Split each sum-type AST node (Term, TypeExpr, PredExpr, FuncExpr, IfAtom,
ThenAtom, Stmt) into one arena node per variant, each with its own typed
id. The generic id (TermId, etc.) still exists as a variant-agnostic
handle; `ast.term(id)` dispatches on the node discriminant and returns
an enum wrapping the specific variant id. Variant ids convert back to
the generic id via `From` so that callers can pass a specific id wherever
a generic one is expected.

Equality and predicate atoms are now shared between if and then atoms:
the same `EqualAtomId` / `PredAtomId` can appear under either context,
and the enclosing `IfStmt` / `ThenStmt` records which.
